{
 "name": "lasso_throw",
 "about": "The lasso: the right hand circles over the head `spins` times (a reach round a ring, 8 points a turn, `per` seconds a point, up to 4 turns), the loop gripped, the body leaning with it; at the end of the last turn the arm whips forward and down for the throw with the fingers opening; then both hands take the rope and he leans back and hauls. The rope is the card's (the right hand is where its end is). Standing or flying (no ground is set). Ends hauling. Plays `base` (IdleBreathe) under it from the start, so the take has a clip of its own and nothing adds up when it is baked or played alone (base 0 leaves what plays underneath).",
